// enum member as JSON, then validates the TypeScript it emits against that
// ground truth (catching operator-precedence mistakes introduced by copying
// Go expression text into TypeScript verbatim).
//
// Here that program becomes `enum_values()` + `print_enum_values_json()`;
// nothing in the crate consumes them yet — a Rust port of the
// `generate:enums` harness calls them the same way `go run` did. Go's
// `encoding/json` sorts map keys and `Encoder.Encode` appends '\n';
// `BTreeMap` iteration order plus `serde_json` reproduce the same bytes.
//
// `.0 as i32` / `X as i32` mirror Go's `toInt32`: the u32/u16 flag payloads
// truncate via `as` exactly the way Go's runtime conversion truncates (flags
// built with a leading bitwise-not), while fieldless enums cast straight
// across.
